{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SamlIdpSlot"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" is never written: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses it locally, before any request, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation failure (CONTRACT.md §34.2 P12.2, contract 1.60 A4) — never as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\""},{"type":"text","text":", never left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the server to refuse. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over thes